    "_about": "THE AMERICAN BISON (Bison bison; 2026-11-08, generator tools/creaturegen/ungulates/gen.py, a cattle rig): a bull of about 1.9 m at the hump, ONE MASS -- the huge head carried low, its forehead almost upright, rising through the crest into the HUMP that peaks over the forelegs, the back sloping evenly down to small, low, round hindquarters in short paler hair (big blends, no step). The dark CAPE is matte coarse wool (`coarse`, `hair`), its colour fading into the body's over ~20 cm (`kc`) with scattered patches of it (paints) past an irregular edge of thinning lumps over the ribs; its SHAGGY OUTLINE is field lumps of many sizes -- along the hump, the SKIRT hanging under the throat, chest and elbows, the CHAPS round the forearms down to the knees, a thick BEARD of rounded locks (longer on the bull), a big curly FORELOCK mat over the brow. Thick forelegs, sturdy hind legs (the ox's, thickened). The HORNS short, sharp and black (`horn`s) from the sides of the head under the mat, out, up and curving in; small ears (the ox's leaf) mostly hidden; small eyes in the wool; a short `sweep` tail with a dark tuft."
  },
